# An axis subscript works on any function by one rule (A6): `f_k X`
# moves axis k of X to the front, applies f (which works on the leading
# axis) and moves it back. A result that lost the leading axis (as a
# reduce does) stays as it is. On a dyadic function the axis is the
# right (data) argument's. `f_1` is f.
== SOURCE
m := 2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6
